  "id": "diabetes-insipidus",
  "term": "diabetes insipidus",
  "definition": "Diabetes insipidus is a biological disease marked by frequent urination, passing large amounts of dilute urine, and excessive thirst. It can result from too little antidiuretic hormone, poor kidney response to that hormone, or problems in hypothalamic control of thirst.",
